{"name":"Late Afternoon","hex":"#f8ab33","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"late","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Near the end of a period of time.","Specifically, near the end of the day."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shift (scheduled work period) that takes place late in the day or at night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/late"},{"term":"afternoon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of the day from noon or lunchtime until sunset, evening, or suppertime or 6pm.","The later part of anything, often with implications of decline."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In the afternoon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afternoon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Late Afternoon","blocks":[{"text":"Late Afternoon is an Irish animated short film directed by Louise Bagnall and produced by Cartoon Saloon."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/91/Late_Afternoon_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Late_Afternoon","wikidata":"Q61022260"},{"title":"Afternoon","blocks":[{"text":"Afternoon is the period from noon to sunset or evening. It is the time when the sun is descending from its peak in the sky to somewhat before its terminus at the horizon in the west. In human life, it occupies roughly the latter half of the standard work and school day. In literal terms, it refers to a time specifically after noon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg/330px-Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afternoon","wikidata":"Q283102"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropolitan_Museum_Of_Art_%285894065780%29.jpg/500px-Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropolitan_